  "question": {
    "text": "If earth has a mass nine times and radius twice to the of a planet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> will be the minimum velocity required by a rocket to pull out of gravitational force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, where ve is escape velocity on earth. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is",
